        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "17177311-31bf-505c-b909-9b9f1e9d60f1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Giuseppe Verdi, Salvadore Cammarano, Antonio García Gutiérrez, Giacomo Puccini, Giuseppe Adami, Alfred Maria Willner, Pietro Neri-Baraldi, Antonietta Fricci\n- Works: Il trovatore, El trovador, La rondine, Rigoletto, Elena da Feltre\n- Organizations: Teatro del Corso\n- Places: Bologna\n- Roles: Manrico, Duke of Mantua, Ubaldo\n\nFacts:\n- In 1836, Antonio García Gutiérrez wrote the play \"El trovador.\"\n- \"Il trovatore\" is an opera in four acts by Giuseppe Verdi with an Italian libretto largely written by Salvadore Cammarano and based on Antonio García Gutiérrez's 1836 play \"El trovador.\"\n- By 1853, Pietro Neri-Baraldi was engaged as the leading tenor at the Teatro del Corso.\n- In 1853, Pietro Neri-Baraldi sang in the first Bologna performances of \"Il trovatore\" as Manrico, \"Rigoletto\" as the Duke of Mantua, and \"Elena da Feltre\" as Ubaldo.\n- Antonietta Fricci was married to the Italian tenor Pietro Neri-Baraldi from 1863 until his death in 1902.\n- \"La rondine\" is an opera in three acts by Giacomo Puccini with an Italian libretto by Giuseppe Adami based on a libretto by Alfred Maria Willner.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "b15fde79-e61a-51c7-b90a-152e7afadd59",
        "text": "Page: Il trovatore. Sentence: Il trovatore (] ; Italian for \"The Troubadour\") is an opera in four acts by Giuseppe Verdi to an Italian libretto largely written by Salvadore Cammarano, based on the play \"El trovador\" (1836) by Antonio García Gutiérrez.\nPage: La rondine. Sentence: La rondine (\"The Swallow\") is an opera in three acts by Giacomo Puccini to an Italian libretto by Giuseppe Adami, based on a libretto by Alfred Maria Willner and .\nPage: Pietro Neri-Baraldi. Sentence: By 1853 he was engaged as the leading tenor at the Teatro del Corso where he sang in the first performances in Bologna of \"Il trovatore\" (as Manrico), \"Rigoletto\" (as the Duke of Mantua), and \"Elena da Feltre\" (as Ubaldo).\nPage: Antonietta Fricci. Sentence: She was married to the Italian tenor Pietro Neri-Baraldi from 1863 until his death in 1902.",
